<span id="A5.p80.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:48.67em;">
<span id="A5.p80.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p80.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;expert_llm_guidance&gt;
<br class="ltx_break">You need to look at the MpmathPrinter class since that’s what’s used when modules=’mpmath’. Let’s examine the implementation:
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">1. First, check the MpmathPrinter in sympy/printing/pycode.py:
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">2. Then look for the _print_Rational method in this class or its parent classes. If MpmathPrinter doesn’t override _print_Rational, check its parent class (likely PythonCodePrinter):
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">3. The issue is likely that the _print_Rational method in PythonCodePrinter (or whatever parent class) is not properly wrapping rational numbers in mpmath.mpf() when used with the mpmath module. You’ll need to modify the MpmathPrinter class to override _print_Rational to use mpmath.mpf() for proper precision.
<br class="ltx_break">&lt;/expert_llm_guidance&gt;
</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
